{"key": "bc7d273d9f15f1a2a5125ce6a9ed913852615269729e179a772422db888f82d3", "value": {"response": "```python\ndef add(lst):\n    \"\"\"Given a non-empty list of integers lst. add the even elements that are at odd indices.\n\n    Examples:\n        add([4, 2, 6, 7]) ==> 2 \n    \"\"\"\n    if not lst or len(lst) < 2:\n        return 0\n\n    # Filter even elements at odd indices\n    result = sum(x for i, x in enumerate(lst) if i % 2 != 0 and x % 2 == 0)\n    return result\n```", "prompt_eval_count": 635, "eval_count": 113}}
